# General Development Principles

- Prioritize maintainability, readability and correctness.
- Do not introduce unnecessary abstractions.
- Do not duplicate existing functionality.
- Before implementing anything, inspect the relevant parts of the codebase.
- Do not modify unrelated files.
- Prefer small, incremental changes.
- Do not silently change existing behavior.
- Explain architectural decisions when they are not obvious.
- Never assume that a feature works without testing it.
- Do not add dependencies without explaining why they are needed.
- If requirements are ambiguous, ask before making architectural decisions.
- Do not make assumptions about future functionality.